---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', url: '/en/' },
  { label: 'Blog', url: '/en/blog/' },
  { label: 'Senior Cat Care', url: '/en/blog/senior-cat-care/' }
];

const siteUrl = 'https://www.petaginghub.com';
const hrefLangAlternates = [
  { lang: 'zh-TW', url: siteUrl + '/blog/senior-cat-care' },
  { lang: 'en', url: siteUrl + '/en/blog/senior-cat-care' },
  { lang: 'x-default', url: siteUrl + '/blog/senior-cat-care' },
];
const faqs = [
  ['When is a cat considered senior?', 'The AAHA/AAFP age-related framework describes cats over 10 as senior. Aging is gradual, and individual health and care needs vary.'],
  ['What changes should I discuss with my veterinarian as my cat ages?', 'Discuss meaningful changes in appetite, weight, thirst, litter-box habits, movement, grooming, sleep, behavior, hearing, or vision. Sudden or severe changes warrant prompt professional advice.'],
  ['How can I make my home easier for an older cat?', 'Helpful adjustments may include accessible food, water, litter boxes, and resting areas; warm quiet sleeping spots; and gradual, predictable routines.'],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Senior Cat Care: Life Stage, Comfort, and Vet Questions"
  description="A practical, educational guide to senior cat care: life-stage context, changes to discuss with a veterinarian, home comfort, and daily routines."
  lang="en"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  hrefLangAlternates={hrefLangAlternates}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-10 px-4">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <span class="inline-block bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-4">Cats</span>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-4">Senior Cat Care: A Complete Guide</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Older cats can remain curious, social, and comfortable for many years. The most useful approach is to notice changes early and discuss your individual cat’s needs with a veterinarian.</p>
    </header>

    <img
      src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513360371669-4adf3dd7dff8?w=1200&h=675&fit=crop&fm=webp"
      alt="A calm cat resting indoors"
      class="w-full aspect-video object-cover rounded-2xl mb-10"
      loading="eager"
    />

    <div class="space-y-10">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">When Is a Cat Considered Senior?</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Aging is individual, but veterinary life-stage guidance commonly describes cats over 10 years old as senior. Calendar age is only one piece of the picture: health history, weight, mobility, behavior, and home environment all matter too.</p>
        <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">Our <a href="/en/tools/cat-age-calculator/" class="text-blue-600 underline">Cat Age Calculator</a> offers a general educational estimate of human-age equivalence. It cannot tell you whether a particular cat is healthy or diagnose a condition.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Changes Worth Discussing With a Veterinarian</h2>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-700 text-sm">
            <li>Changes in appetite, body weight, thirst, or litter-box habits</li>
            <li>Reduced jumping, stiffness, altered grooming, or changes in activity</li>
            <li>New sleep, vocalization, or social behavior changes</li>
          </ul>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-700 text-sm">
            <li>Changes in vision, hearing, or apparent orientation</li>
            <li>Dental discomfort, persistent bad breath, or difficulty eating</li>
            <li>Any sudden, severe, or concerning change from your cat’s usual behavior</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-4">Cats can be subtle communicators. A short record of what has changed and when can make a veterinary visit more useful. See our <a href="/en/blog/cat-aging-signs/" class="text-blue-600 underline">signs of aging in cats guide</a> for more educational context.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Create a Senior-Friendly Home</h2>
        <div class="bg-purple-50 rounded-2xl p-5 border border-purple-100">
          <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-700 text-sm">
            <li><strong>Make essentials easy to reach:</strong> Keep water, food, litter boxes, and resting areas accessible without difficult jumps.</li>
            <li><strong>Offer comfortable rest:</strong> Provide warm, quiet sleeping areas away from busy walkways.</li>
            <li><strong>Consider low-entry options:</strong> A low-entry litter box or stable step can be helpful if movement becomes difficult.</li>
            <li><strong>Keep the environment predictable:</strong> Gentle routines and gradual changes can be easier for many older cats.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">Questions for a Senior-Cat Wellness Visit</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-700">
          <li>What life stage do you consider my cat to be in?</li>
          <li>How often should my individual cat have wellness visits?</li>
          <li>Which changes in mobility, grooming, eating, thirst, or litter-box habits should prompt a call?</li>
          <li>Are there home, nutrition, or routine changes that suit my cat’s specific needs?</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
      <a href="/en/tools/cat-age-calculator/" class="px-5 py-3 bg-purple-500 hover:bg-purple-600 text-white font-semibold rounded-xl text-sm">Cat Age Calculator</a>
      <a href="/en/blog/senior-pet-health-guide/" class="px-5 py-3 bg-purple-100 hover:bg-purple-200 text-purple-800 font-semibold rounded-xl text-sm">Senior Pet Health Guide</a>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-8"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Frequently asked questions</h2>{faqs.map(([q,a]) => <details class="py-3 border-b"><summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-blue-600">{q}</summary><p class="mt-3 text-slate-700">{a}</p></details>)}</section>
    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-slate-600">Sources: <a class="text-blue-700 underline" href="https://www.aaha.org/resources/2021-aaha-aafp-feline-life-stage-guidelines/feline-life-stage-definitions/">AAHA/AAFP life-stage definitions</a>; <a class="text-blue-700 underline" href="https://www.vet.cornell.edu/departments-centers-and-institutes/cornell-feline-health-center/health-information/feline-health-topics/special-needs-senior-cat">Cornell senior cat care</a>. The age estimate cannot assess health.</p>
    <p class="mt-10 text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed"><strong>Educational note:</strong> This page provides general information only. It does not diagnose illness or replace an examination or advice from a veterinarian. Contact a veterinary professional promptly for sudden, severe, or concerning changes.</p>
  </article>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: faqs.map(([name, text]) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text } }))
  })} />
</BaseLayout>
